* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* COMPARES(array1, array2 {, justification})
*
* The multivalued form of COMPARE(): every element of array1 is compared with the element of array2 in the same place and the
* result, -1, 0 or 1, is put in the same place in the answer.  An array that has no element at a place gives a null string
* there.  The justification is as for COMPARE(): L (the default) or R, and an I after it makes the comparison case blind.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

function !compares(array1, array2, just) var.args
$catalog !compares

   jst = 'L'
   if arg.present(just) then
      if just # '' then jst = just
   end

   result = ''
   nf = max(dcount(array1, @fm), dcount(array2, @fm))
   for f = 1 to nf
      nv = max(dcount(array1<f>, @vm), dcount(array2<f>, @vm))
      for v = 1 to nv
         ns = max(dcount(array1<f,v>, @svm), dcount(array2<f,v>, @svm))
         for s = 1 to ns
            result<f,v,s> = compare(array1<f,v,s>, array2<f,v,s>, jst)
         next s
      next v
   next f

   return result
end

* END-CODE
